DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The aaggpp driver provides support for programming the AGP GART.  This sup‐
     port is used by drm(4) kernel drivers.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     drm(4), inteldrm(4), radeondrm(4), vga(4)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The aaggpp driver first appeared in FreeBSD 4.1.  It was adopted in
     NetBSD 1.6.  The driver was then ported in parts to OpenBSD, and fully
     integrated in OpenBSD 4.3.  The userland ioctl(2) interface was removed
     in OpenBSD 5.6.

